    "created_at": "2015-09-25T14:07:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-25T14:07:11Z",
    "body": "An alternate way of wording the spec would be to have the scroll to a fragment algorithm set a \"current target\" field on the document, and then we just do a comparison for matching the selector.\n\nBrowsers diverge on what happens when an element is removed from the DOM. Gecko continues to match it (when reinserted), whereas Blink does not.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
